 "text": " What if a chicken lost its head and just kept living? September 10th, 1945, Fruta, Colorado. Farmer Lloyd Olsen picks a rooster for dinner. His mother-in-law loves the neck, so he aims the axe high. The head comes off, and the rooster gets up and wanders away. The blade had missed the brain stem, the part that runs breathing and digestion. So the Olsons fed him milk and water with an eyedropper and cleared his throat with a syringe. They named him Mike. Mike went on tour across America. People paid 25 cents to see him. Time and Life magazines wrote about him. He lived for 18 months with no head. Then, in March 1947, in a Phoenix motel, Mike choked in the night. The syringe had been left behind at the show. Today, his hometown throws him a festival every year, and Guinness still lists his record. Subscribe for more weird facts.",
